---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms — Lrnon"
  description="Plain-language terms: the learning is free forever, lessons are CC BY-SA 4.0, code is MIT, and course content is education, not professional advice.">
  <section class="container prose" style="padding-block:var(--sp-12);">
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-500);">Terms of use</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--c-ink-soft);">Version 0.1 · public preview · last updated 2026-07-09</p>

    <h2>Free means free</h2>
    <p>All learning content on this platform is free, with no paywalls, paid
    tiers, or paid certificates — as a standing commitment, not a promotion.</p>

    <h2>Licences</h2>
    <p>Lessons and learning content: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>
    (share and adapt with attribution, same licence). Platform code: MIT,
    in the public repository. You are explicitly welcome to fork all of it.</p>

    <h2>What this isn't</h2>
    <p>Course content is education about AI tools and concepts. It is not
    legal, medical, financial, or professional advice, and third-party tools
    it describes change frequently — verify specifics against official
    documentation (our lessons teach exactly this habit).</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>The platform is provided as-is, in active development, without
    warranties of any kind. We aim for accuracy and mark every lesson and
    tool card with a verification date so you can judge freshness yourself.</p>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>Anyone can learn here, at any age, subject to the law where you live.
    Learning without an account processes no personal data at all, so there is
    nothing to consent to.</p>
    <p>Creating an account or volunteering does involve personal data — an email
    address at minimum. If you are under 18, we need a parent or guardian's
    confirmation by email before either goes ahead, and they can withdraw it at
    any time. The <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> sets out exactly how that
    works and what we keep.</p>

    <h2>Be decent</h2>
    <p>Don't abuse the service, attempt to disrupt it for others, or
    misrepresent your relationship with the project. That's the whole list.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
